# Dotfiles / bootstrap (agent)

Human docs: `README.md`. WSL pitfalls: `wsl-bootstrap.mdc`.

## Architecture
- Declarative first (`dot_*`, `private_*`, `dot_config/...`); scripts last.
- `run_once_*` / `run_onchange_*`: small, idempotent; packages/migrations only.
- One bootstrap style: `bootstrap.ps1` / `bootstrap.sh` → tool → init/apply|update → optional SSH. No second entry path.
- Ship Linux + Windows unless OS-specific; templates only for real OS/host diffs.
- Secrets stay local (`config.d`, chezmoi config, password managers). Migrations backup first (`run_once_*`).

## Dependencies
- Pin self-installed binaries in `.chezmoidata.toml` `[packages]`; float apt (`zsh`, `fzf`, …).
- Preferred + floor when PPAs lag: `git` + `git_minimum` (≥ 2.35 for `zdiff3`).
- Current pins: `chezmoi`, `oh_my_posh`, `git`, `git_minimum` — bump in data file, not hardcoded elsewhere.
- New pin: (1) data file (2) `run_onchange_*` or bootstrap install (3) soft-fail in profiles — never `eval` broken init (4) CI asset check when practical.
- Downloads: prefer winget/apt when exact; else GitHub release → `$HOME/.cache/...`, retry, checksum, `~/.local/bin`. No bare `curl | sh` for critical bins on flaky WSL.
- Scripts must be re-runnable (skip if desired version present).

## Validation
- Entry: `bash ./scripts/ci-check.sh` (no `just` yet). CI: shellcheck, chezmoi dry-run, template renders, pin reachability, PowerShell parse.
- Bootstrap “failed” wrappers only mirror child exit — reproduce with `bash -x` / PS tracing in-target.

## Backlog (same patterns)
- Good later: pinned `direnv`/`mise`; optional password-manager `IdentityAgent`; richer fzf helpers without plugin frameworks.
- Skip: plugin frameworks, package sprawl, in-repo private keys, per-host secret sync.
